        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): strip runtime stream-boundary markers from user-visible text",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem**: Runtime stream-boundary markers (`[e~[` / `[e[`) leak as trailing suffix in user-visible channel deliveries (reported on Telegram with MiniMax/MiniMax-M3). Fixes #105113.\n\n**Solution**: Add `stripRuntimeStreamMarkers` to the `sanitizeUserFacingText` pipeline with **trailing-suffix-only** regexes (narrower fix addressing ClawSweeper regex-breadth concerns).\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nValidates actual production `sanitizeUserFacingText` function:\n\n```\n$ npx tsx _validate-stream-markers.mts\n=== sanitizeUserFacingText — stream marker stripping ===\n\n  ✓ trailing [e~[ stripped\n    input:  \"Hello world[e~[\"\n    output: \"Hello world\"\n  ✓ trailing [e[ stripped (no tilde)\n    input:  \"Test output[e[\"\n    output: \"Test output\"\n  ✓ trailing lone [ after whitespace stripped\n    input:  \"Partial reply [\"\n    output: \"Partial reply\"\n  ✓ mid-text [e~[ with trailing newline — preserved (suffix-only regex)\n    input:  \"Result[e~[\\nNext line\"\n    output: \"Result[e~[\\nNext line\"\n  ✓ inline [e~[ preserved (not at end)\n    input:  \"The marker [e~[ is used for streaming\"\n    output: \"The marker [e~[ is used for streaming\"\n  ✓ inline [e[ preserved (not at end)\n    input:  \"Markers like [e[ appear mid-text\"\n    output: \"Markers like [e[ appear mid-text\"\n  ✓ normal text unchanged\n    input:  \"Hello, this is a normal response.\"\n    output: \"Hello, this is a normal response.\"\n  ✓ empty string unchanged\n    input:  \"\"\n    output: \"\"\n\n✅ 8 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- Existing `sanitizeUserFacingText` test suite passes\n- Focused test file `sanitizeuserfacingtext.test.ts` covers trailing marker stripping and inline preservation\n\n/cc @openclaw/clawsweeper",
